[stderr] # Implementation catalogue index
[stderr] 
[stderr] This is the F012 implementation-authoring index for **mock-fantasy-quest-4**.
[stderr] The machine-readable source is
[stderr] [`implementation-catalogue-index.json`](implementation-catalogue-index.json).
[stderr] It decomposes only the first bounded shard; it does not author R-series
[stderr] runbooks or approve any decision gate.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Scope and ownership rules
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **SHARD-01 — Foundation and core contracts** contains 12 independently
[stderr]   verifiable contracts (limit: 250). It establishes framework-neutral seams,
[stderr]   deterministic data contracts, local persistence/recovery protocols, quality
[stderr]   controls, and documentation. It does not implement campaign behaviour,
[stderr]   player UI, PWA lifecycle, or release actions.
[stderr] - **Shared** owns campaign rules and platform-neutral contracts. **Web** owns
[stderr]   browser input, responsive layout, origin storage, and web builds. **PWA** is
[stderr]   a delivery/cache/install adaptation only: it reuses the shared game and web
[stderr]   UI, while owning its service-worker lifecycle. Save data and cache data are
[stderr]   deliberately separate.
[stderr] - `GATE-*` records block dependent authoring; they are not defaults. The
[stderr]   catalogue keeps connected capabilities out of P0 under `GATE-0006`.
[stderr] - Content must be original. The functional reference never authorises copied
[stderr]   names, text, lore, art, maps, layouts, music, or interaction choreography.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Current contracts
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Domain | Outcome | Prerequisites | Gate/status |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | IMP-0001 | Foundation | Reproducible shared project baseline | — | GATE-0001 / gated |
[stderr] | IMP-0002 | Foundation | Core and adapter dependency seams | IMP-0001 | current |
[stderr] | IMP-0003 | Tests | Deterministic test/fixture harness | IMP-0001–0002 | current |
[stderr] | IMP-0004 | Data | Deterministic state/command/event contract | IMP-0002–0003 | current |
[stderr] | IMP-0005 | Content | Versioned content schema and validator | IMP-0001, 0003–0004 | current |
[stderr] | IMP-0006 | Persistence | Local save/recovery protocol | IMP-0002–0004 | GATE-0003 / gated |
[stderr] | IMP-0007 | Persistence | Pure migration runner | IMP-0005–0006 | GATE-0003 / gated |
[stderr] | IMP-0008 | Security | P0 connected-service exclusions | IMP-0002, 0004 | current |
[stderr] | IMP-0009 | Privacy | Local, redacted diagnostics boundary | IMP-0002–0003, 0006 | GATE-0005 / gated |
[stderr] | IMP-0010 | Accessibility | Semantic design-token contract | IMP-0001–0002 | GATE-0002/0004 / gated |
[stderr] | IMP-0011 | Content | Original-content provenance control | IMP-0005 | current + human review |
[stderr] | IMP-0012 | Documentation | Foundation boundary documentation | IMP-0002, 0004, 0006, 0008 | current |
[stderr] 
[stderr] Each JSON contract has one title, domain, target allocation, requirement IDs,
[stderr] bounded outcome, prerequisite list, sole files/data/API ownership, forbidden
[stderr] scope, verification, human/external gate, complexity, and status. The only
[stderr] dependency direction is toward earlier contracts, so the current graph is
[stderr] acyclic.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Domain-expansion queue
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Queue ID | Bounded domain (maximum contracts) | Dependency | Requirements/gate | Allocation |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | SHARD-02 | Campaign content and domain logic (250) | SHARD-01 | Core P0 campaign; GATE-0004 | Shared core/content; no UI |
[stderr] | SHARD-03 | Session, UI, input, and accessibility (250) | SHARD-01–02 | REQ-0005–0007, 0009–0010, 0012; GATE-0002–0004 | Shared UI model, Web adapters, inherited PWA UI |
[stderr] | SHARD-04 | PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence (250) | SHARD-01–03 | REQ-0011–0012, NFR-0001/0003/0006/0009/0011/0012; GATE-0002/0005/0007 | Separate web build and PWA lifecycle |
[stderr] | SHARD-05 | Connected-scope decision package (250) | SHARD-01 | REQ-0014–0015; GATE-0006 | Hold; research/decision outputs only if authorised |
[stderr] 
